b5c0b95..d30dc3a preserves legacy sampler output: d30dc3a is c153e01 (covered by b5c0b95-0c08180) plus one src/ change, 68e02c4, which bounds the reflections each window's `:adaptive` fit adds at `max_reflections=16` and rewrites the reflection metric product without per-reflection copies. The product is bit-identical (the same contiguous BLAS `dot` on the same gathered values; test/matrix_expressions.jl compares it with the former implementation bit for bit), and the bound only changes a fit that would add more than 16 reflections, which no measured real target does. The paired reparam driver runs here match outside timing and provenance.

Evidence: docs/benchmark/run_reparam_benchmark.jl with WHMC_BENCH_TARGETS=funnel,eight_schools-eight_schools_centered,seeds_data-seeds_centered_model,radon_mn-radon_partially_pooled_centered,radon_mn-radon_variable_intercept_centered, WHMC_BENCH_SEEDS=1 and WHMC_BENCH_DRAWS=1000 (WHMC_BENCH_AD unset): 23 runs per side, 0 failed. It was run on gordito on 2026-10-22 with Julia 1.10.12, at both clean WarmupHMC revisions, each in its own clone with docs/benchmark resolved against that clone through resolve_script (the resolver developed each clone's own root). before/ and after/ preserve the full driver outputs.

Why the bound does not reach the other harnesses: every window refit of 15 posteriordb models plus Neal's funnel (4 seeds, 106 refits, branch kb-impl/WarmupHMC-two-stage-tsvd at 5742c26, driver docs/benchmark/two_stage_tsvd_refits.jl there) added at most 7 reflections; linear_restart.json records at most 5 adaptive reflections on its targets (diamonds, kilpisjarvi, 8-dimensional Gaussians). The BRM inventory artifacts do not record reflection counts; their models are hierarchical regressions of the kind measured above, which is the claim this record rests on for them.
